'''Palmo Plaza''',<ref name="Trivia">{{SW|url=news/andor-trivia-guide-week-2|text=Secrets from the Set of ''Andor'' Season 2: Week 2 Trivia}}</ref> also known as the '''Ghorman Plaza''',<ref name="Welcome to the Rebellion">{{Andor|Welcome to the Rebellion}}</ref> was a central<ref name="7ways">{{SW|url=news/how-andor-changes-how-we-view-rogue-one|text=7 Ways ''Andor'' Changes How We Watch ''Rogue One: A Star Wars Story''}}</ref> open space in the [[city]] of [[Palmo]] on the [[planet]] [[Ghorman]]. In the middle of the plaza stood the [[Monument to the Fallen]], a memorial to the victims of the [[Tarkin Massacre]].<ref name="Ever Been" /> In [[2 BBY]], the [[Ghorman Massacre]] occurred in the plaza when hundreds of [[Ghorman (people)|Ghorman people]] assembled to protest the occupying [[Galactic Empire]]'s tyranny. As the shooting began, Imperial [[stormtrooper]]s fired on civilians, and members of the rebel [[Ghorman Front]] attempted to fight back. Hundreds were [[Death|killed]] during the event, which the Empire orchestrated in order to arrange their takeover of the planet.<ref name="WAY" />

==Description==
===Composition===
Palmo Plaza was a plaza located in [[Palmo]], the [[capital]] of the [[planet]] [[Ghorman]]. The plaza was located in the center of the [[city]], and was a spot for both gatherings and protest for many [[Ghorman (people)|Ghormans]] living in the city.

===Monument to the Fallen===
Situated in the center or the plaza, the [[Monument to the Fallen]] was a monument dedicated to those crushed and killed in the [[Tarkin Massacre]], an event in which [[Grand Moff|grand moff]] [[Wilhuff Tarkin|Tarkin]] attempted to land his cruiser in that very spot, ignoring the Ghorman people protesting the [[Galactic Empire]] beneath it.

The monument was a common spot used by members of the [[Ghorman Front]] to spread awareness to the tyranny of the empire and sway people to their cause.

===Palmo Plaza hotel===
{{Main|Palmo Plaza hotel}}
{{Quote|Holo-screen, air flow and window blinds, they all work through the single console on the nightstand.|Thela, showing Cassian Andor his room in the hotel|<ref name="I Have Friends Everywhere">{{Andor|I Have Friends Everywhere}}</ref>}}

Built into Palmo Plaza, the '''Palmo Plaza hotel''' was an upscale hotel for those visiting [[Ghorman]]. Cassian Andor stayed at this hotel multiple times under fake aliases while visiting Ghorman.<ref name="I Have Friends Everywhere">{{Andor|I Have Friends Everywhere}}</ref><ref name=":0">{{Andor|Messenger}}</ref>

===Ghorman cafe===
{{Main|Ghorman cafe}}
{{Quote|Wilmon! Tell me where you are!''"<br />"''West side. The columns by the cafhouse.|Cassian Andor and Wilmon Paak|<ref name="WAY" />}}

the '''Ghorman Cafhouse''' was a [[Cafe|cafhouse]] located in the west side of Palmo Plaza. Cassian Andor met with a member of the [[Ghorman Front]] at the cafhouse.<ref name="Ever Been" />

===Imperial office complex===
{{Main|Imperial office complex}}
The [[Imperial office complex]] was a office complex located partially within Palmo Plaza. By [[3 BBY]], The complex served as the administrative hub for the [[Galactic Empire]] on [[Ghorman]] during Dedra Meero's reign over the [[planet]].<ref name=":0" /><ref name=":1">{{Andor|Who Are You?}}</ref>

The complex had offices dedicated to organizations within the Galactic Empire such as the [[Imperial Bureau of Standards]], which had a [[Bureau of Standards Ghorman field office|office]] within the complex.<ref name="Ever Been" />

===South Steps===
The South Steps were a set of stairs at the south side of the plaza that lead to the second floor of the plaza. During the [[Ghorman Massacre]], a [[South Steps Unit|unit]] of [[stormtrooper]]s were deployed at the steps that eventually opened fire on protesters.<ref name=":1" />

==Behind the scenes==
[[File:GhormanMassacreMindMap.jpg|thumb|250px|A mind map used by ''Andor'' editor [[Yan Miles]] for the Ghorman Massacre in the episode "Who Are You?"]]
Palmo Plaza appeared in the [[Andor Season 2|second season]] of the live-action series ''[[Star Wars: Andor]]'', first appearing in the season's forth episode, "[[Ever Been to Ghorman?]]," which was released on [[Disney+]]<ref name="Ever Been" /> on [[April 29]], [[2025]].<ref name="Trailer News">{{SW|url=news/andor-season-2-teaser-trailer-key-art-reveal|text=First ''Andor A Star Wars Story'' Teaser Trailer and Poster Revealed}}</ref>

The plaza formed the largest set built for ''Andor'' at [[Pinewood Studios]] in England. According to executive producer [[Sanne Wohlenberg]], it was designed with the development of the Imperial crackdown in mind, effectively making the plaza with "no way out" for the demonstrators during the Ghorman Massacre.<ref name="Built to be destroyed">{{YouTube|url=U7biyc3ANiQ|text=Ghorman, Built to Be Destroyed &#124; Tony Gilroy & ANDOR Filmmakers Break Down the Massacre &#124; Deep Dive|channel=@indiewire|name=Indie Wire|date=2025-06-17|archivedate=20250618214151}}</ref>

